speechtext:
3.	The modifications made to the telephone were highly professional and covert. Sophisticated equipment would be used at the listening post in order to decrease detection from the user and the telephone company.
4.	All phones should be scanned and proper safeguards taken against illegal intrusion devices.
5.	The following characteristics would apply to the kind of listening device which could be operated with these modifications to the boardroom telephone:
Life span: until removed from the phone;
Installation time: 5-10 minutes;
Listening capabilities: whatever was said in the boardroom;
Detection: does not affect normal operation of phone, only detected by use of electronic equipment and hard physical inspection;
Listening post: within telephone network, with harmonica or infinity transmitter, ultimately receivable virtually anywhere in the world (with exception of Germany);
Popularity: Utilized by professionals in the intelligence gathering field.
W. M. Sandiford	Dan McGarry
General Manager	President
Uniserv Sound & Signal Inc. Uniserv Sound & Signal Inc.
